296
00:10:14,041 --> 00:10:16,662
fifty billion dollars in its next quarter

297
00:10:16,662 --> 00:10:17,739
alone.

298
00:10:17,983 --> 00:10:20,614
So here is the one number to

299
00:10:20,614 --> 00:10:21,353
watch.

300
00:10:21,353 --> 00:10:22,683
Not the spending.

301
00:10:22,683 --> 00:10:24,233
The backlog.

302
00:10:24,233 --> 00:10:26,412
As long as customers keep signing

303
00:10:26,412 --> 00:10:28,833
contracts faster than the companies can

304
00:10:28,833 --> 00:10:29,293
build,

305
00:10:29,293 --> 00:10:31,083
the bet is paying off.

306
00:10:31,083 --> 00:10:33,510
If the backlog stops growing while the

307
00:10:33,510 --> 00:10:34,942
spending keeps rising,

308
00:10:34,942 --> 00:10:37,854
the data centers become very expensive

309
00:10:37,854 --> 00:10:39,182
empty rooms.

310
00:10:39,417 --> 00:10:41,524
So how does Big Tech really make

311
00:10:41,524 --> 00:10:43,177
money from AI?

312
00:10:43,357 --> 00:10:45,192
By renting the machines,

313
00:10:45,192 --> 00:10:46,794
by selling better ads,

314
00:10:46,794 --> 00:10:49,717
and by locking in customers for years.

315
00:10:49,737 --> 00:10:52,497
The chatbot is the shop window.

316
00:10:52,587 --> 00:10:54,817
The real business is behind it,

317
00:10:54,817 --> 00:10:56,372
in the data centers,

318
00:10:56,372 --> 00:10:57,701
in the ad auctions,

319
00:10:57,701 --> 00:10:59,503
and in contracts that will pay out

320
00:10:59,503 --> 00:11:02,581
long after the next model is released.

321
00:11:02,817 --> 00:11:05,315
Next time on The Hidden Economics,

322
00:11:05,315 --> 00:11:08,294
we follow the money behind another hidden

323
00:11:08,294 --> 00:11:10,727
link of the world economy.

324
00:11:10,837 --> 00:11:13,271
This is The Hidden Economics.
